tance from the ukrainian armed  forces  if ukraine were to lose that ability to  at least deny russia control of its  airspace then russia would be able to to  roam freely across ukraine from another  point of view and that changes the tenor  of this campaign quite significantly not  only would it allow the russian air  force to target the ukrainian armed  forces and perhaps civilians but also  give the russian command and control  systems their commanders much better  information than they're getting at the  moment  so when i hear people talk about  humanitarian no-fly zone i i kind of  doubt that they know almost what what  that means the issue with no-fly zones  is you have to be prepared to enforce  them so if this humanitarian no-fly zone  was something that was was voluntary for  example then then there'd be no reason  for russia to comply with that no-fly  zone if it chose not to it's a bit like  shelling humanitarian corridors it kind  of promises a thing which perhaps it  can't deliver
 

